<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>The most useful number on this page is not a rate per square metre. It is the minimum job charge. Victorian removalists publish a minimum of <strong>$800 to $1,500</strong> for a residential job, and it explains most of the quotes that catch people off guard. The gap between two cracked sheets off a shed wall and a whole fence line is much smaller than you would expect, because the bulk of the cost is simply getting a licensed crew and a legal disposal load to your address.</p><p>Every figure here comes from Victorian suppliers, councils or national cost guides. None of them is a quote from us, and none is a Geelong rate, because no Geelong or Barwon operator publishes one. Read them as Melbourne metro benchmarks; two of those suppliers price regional work separately anyway. Prices are indicative and GST treatment varies between providers, so ask each removalist whether their quote includes GST.</p></div></div></section>
